From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:28:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] html: mask-image drawn in the background colour

A box with a mask image fetches it like a background image and is drawn as
the image's shapes in the box's background colour (the way sites draw
icons: mask: url(icon.svg) with background-color: currentcolor), fitted
into the padding box and centred (as mask-size: contain; mask-size and
mask-position are not parsed).  There is no compositing: the image is
drawn through plotters that paint its fills and strokes in that colour, so
SVG masks work and bitmaps are drawn as they are.  The box's own
background and borders are not drawn; while the mask loads, or if it
failed, the box shows nothing.  Its contents are drawn unmasked.
---
